R"VG(
# letters_life2.vg (H-04, the second pass): more of the ordinary life between a letter's news (letters_life.vg's `letter.ambient`): the market,
# the other people, the table, the body's complaints, the faith. Each line a part of what happened and a part of how it is taken.

# ---- the market -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

let.market
  (3) {let.market.main}{let.market.tail}
let.market.main (share=0.75)
  {crop} is dear this year {=.dear}
  {crop} is cheap, and the farmers are angry {=.cheap}
  (age<=medieval) salt has gone up again {=.dear}
  (age>=industrial) bread is up again {=.dear}
  (age>=modern) everything costs twice what it did {=.dear}
  (age>=medieval) it is {n} {coin} for {vessel.one} of {food} now {=.dear}
  the traders brought {trade} and took our {crop2} {=.trade}
  the fair was all {craft} and no buyers {=.cheap}
  you can get {fruit} for nothing at the market, they rot so fast this year {=.cheap}
  (age>=medieval) I paid a {smallcoin} for {veg} that were mostly water {=.dear}
  nobody has any {fuel} to sell, and nobody will say why {=.dear}
  the {herd} fetch half what they did {=.cheap}
  we got {n} {measure.load} of {crop} for a cart of {veg}, which nobody thinks was fair {=.trade}
let.market.tail
  (2) .
  (.dear=1) ; we manage.
  (.dear=1) , and nobody knows why.
  (.dear=1) ; the rich are eating {food} and the rest of us are eating it too, but less.
  (.cheap=1) ; good for us, bad for whoever grew it.
  (.trade=1) ; I think we were cheated, and so do they.
  (.cheap=1 contact=1) ; the {other} undersell everyone.

# ---- the other people (C-13) ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

let.other
  (3) {let.other.main}{let.other.tail}
let.other.main (share=0.8)
  the {other} were at the market again, selling {trade} {=.sell}
  one of the {other} has taken the house at the end of the street {=.moved}
  (otherwar=1) nobody will buy from the {other} now, and they will not sell to us {=.war}
  the children have learnt a song of the {other} and will not stop singing it {=.song}
  there was a quarrel with the {other} over the grazing {=.quarrel}
  an old woman of the {other} showed me how they make {food}, and it is better than ours {=.food}
  the {other} keep {herd} too, and theirs are thinner, which pleases everyone {=.sell}
  (othergone=1) there are things of the {other} in every house now, and nobody to ask what they were for {=.gone}
let.other.tail
  (2) .
  (.sell=1) ; their prices are high and their manners good.
  (.moved=1) ; nobody knows what to say to them, so we say good morning.
  (.quarrel=1) ; it was settled, for now.
  (!has:.gone) , and I do not know what to make of them.
  (.food=1) ; do not tell Mother.
  (.war=1) ; it is a stupid business.

# small words the lines share
let.tool.n (people=3)
  adze
  sickle
  hoe
  spindle
  net
  axe
  awl
  scraper
  (age>=medieval) plough
  (age>=medieval) scythe

# ---- the table -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

let.table
  (3) {let.table.main}{let.table.tail}
let.table.main (share=0.75)
  we are living on {food} and {veg} until the {crop} is in {=.thin}
  I made {food} the way Mother did, and it was not the same {=.mother}
  (has:$you) we have {drink} enough for an army, and somebody has to help us with it {=.drink}
  the first {fruit} came to the market today, small and dear {=.first}
  we had {food} at {festival}, and {drink}, and too much of both {=.feast}
  the {crop} bread came out of the oven like a stone {=.stone}
  we dried the {fruit} on the roof, and the {bird} ate half {=.birds}
  (economy=herding|economy2=herding) there is milk and {food} and nothing else, and the children say so daily {=.thin}
  (coast=1) we eat {fish} until we dream of them {=.fish}
  our {drink} went sour this year, and we drink it anyway {=.drink}
  I have learnt to make {food} from the {craft} woman next door {=.learn}
  (age>=industrial) we bought {food} in a tin, and it tasted of the tin {=.tin}
  the {veg} are good this year; it is the only thing that is {=.good}
  (desert=1) the {fruit} came in sweet, and we ate them in the shade with our feet in a {vessel.one.n} of water {=.good}
let.table.tail
  (2) .
  (.thin=1) ; nobody is thin yet, but nobody is fat.
  (.mother=1) ; nothing is.
  (.drink=1) ; it is strong, and nobody will admit how strong.
  (.first=1) ; we bought one each and ate them standing in the street.
  (.stone=1) ; the {beast} would not eat it either.
  (.birds=1) ; the {bird} were fatter than we were by the end.
  (.learn=1) ; it is better than ours, and I will deny that I said so.
  (.tin=1) ; the children loved it.

# ---- the body -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

let.body
  (3) {let.body.main}{let.body.tail}
let.body.main (share=0.75)
  my back is bad again {=.back}
  the cough is going round {$me.home}, and I have it {=.cough}
  I have a tooth that keeps me up at night, and I chew {food} on the other side {=.tooth}
  my eyes are not what they were; I write this large, by the {fuel} {=.eyes}
  I am stronger than last year, which is not saying much, and can carry {vessel.one} up the hill again {=.strong}
  the healer gave me {crop2} steeped in {drink} for the chest {=.cure}
  my knees know the weather before {skyone} does {=.knees}
  (age>=industrial) the doctor says rest, and the work says otherwise {=.doctor}
  I sleep badly; I hear the {herd} in my sleep {=.sleep}
  my hands are stiff in the mornings now, like Father's were {=.hands}
  I fell on the ice by {$me.home.landmark} and the whole street saw {=.fell}
let.body.tail
  (2) .
  (.back=1) ; I carry the {vessel} anyway, because who else will.
  (.cough=1) ; it is nothing, everyone says, and everyone coughs.
  (.tooth=1) ; I will have it out at {festival}, when everyone is too merry to hear.
  (.cure=1) ; it tastes like the floor and it works.
  (.doctor=1) ; I listen to the work.
  (.sleep=1) , which they would find funny.
  (.hands=1) ; I hold them over the {fuel} and they forgive me.
  (.fell=1) ; my pride is worse than my hip.
  (!has:.fell) ; do not worry.

# ---- the faith ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

let.faith
  (3) {let.faith.main}{let.faith.tail}
let.faith.main (share=0.75)
  the priest of {god} has a new way of saying the old words at {holyplace} {=.priest}
  {holyplace} has a new keeper, young and loud {=.keeper}
  we {rite.do} for {festival}, as every year, and ate {food} after {=.rite}
  we had {feast.custom} again, and it rained, as it does {=.feast}
  (faith=ancestors) I said the names of the old ones at the door, and one I had forgotten came back to me {=.names}
  (faith=sky) {skyone} was clear for the feast, which the priests take as approval {=.sky}
  (faith=land) the offering at {holyplace} was {offering}, and the land took it {=.offer}
  (faith=onegod) {god} is in everything, the preacher says, our leaking roof included {=.preach}
  (faith=philosophy) the teachers argued all night at {holyplace} about whether {virtue} can be taught {=.argue}
  (faith=manygods) there is a new god at the market, small and {colour.any} and cheap, and everyone is buying one {=.gods}
  (temper=pious) I went up to {holyplace} early and was alone there with {god} {=.alone}
  (stage>=1) nobody goes to {holyplace} any more except the old and the frightened {=.empty}
  the {colour.holy} cloth at {holyplace} has been renewed, and it is very bright {=.cloth}
let.faith.tail
  (2) .
  (.priest=1) ; everyone hates it.
  (.keeper=1) ; the old ones give it a year.
  (.feast=1) ; we were wet and happy.
  (.names=1) ; I am getting old.
  (.preach=1) ; I said so to the roof.
  (.argue=1) ; it cannot, it seems, or not to them.
  (.gods=1) ; I bought two.
  (.alone=1) ; it was the best hour of {season.this}.
  (.empty=1) ; I am one or the other.

)VG"
